<title>UK: UK Labour utility tax to hit BT, BAA - sources.</title>
<headline>UK Labour utility tax to hit BT, BAA - sources.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-03-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Britain's  opposition Labour Party's planned windfall tax on privatised utilities is likely to be levied on airports operator BAA Plc and British Telecommunications, Labour sources said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>Other companies expected to be affected if Labour wins the May 1 election include Railtrack as well as Britain's gas, water and electricity suppliers, but British Airways is expected to be excluded, the sources said.</p>
</text>
